      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:5:2:40:6",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ النِّثَارِ مِنَ السُّكَّرِ وَ اللَّوْزِ وَ أَشْبَاهِهِ أَ يَحِلُّ أَكْلُهُ قَالَ يُكْرَهُ أَكْلُ مَا انْتُهِبَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Al Amraky Bin Ali, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Ali son of Ja’far<sup>asws</sup>, from his brother<sup>asws</sup> Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup>, said, ‘I asked him<sup>asws</sup> about the confetti of the sugar and the hazel-nuts, and its like, is it Permissible to eat it?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘It is disliked to eat what is seized’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "6. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from al-Nawfaliy from al-Sakuniy who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, would prohibit utilization of walnuts, that children bring after using in gambling, saying that it is Suht (filthy), unlawful.’” "
        ]
      }
